@chapter 19 | Exchange Rate, FDI and External Debt

@intro
This chapter covers the **exchange rate** (flexible rates, rupee **convertibility**, **devaluation**), **remittances**, **foreign direct and portfolio investment** (sectors, sources, caps, participatory notes), **external debt** and **ECBs**, **foreign exchange reserves**, the **euro**, and the move from **FERA to FEMA**. It contains **{pyqs} PYQs and {ones} one-liners**.
@end

@section 19.1 | Exchange Rate and Convertibility

@q 13:1-3

@table
Convertibility step | Year
Partial convertibility (LERMS) | 1992-93
**Current account convertibility** | **August 1994** (IMF Article VIII)
**Capital account convertibility** committees | **Tarapore I (1997)**, **Tarapore II (2006)**; not yet full
Exchange rate regime | **Market-determined** (managed float) since **March 1993**
@end

A **flexible (floating) rate** is set by the **market's** demand for and supply of foreign currency, not by the central bank, though the RBI steps in to smooth swings.

